    "result": "I implemented `EnsureIndex` in `ensure.go` but could not run anything: `go test` and deleting a file both needed approval I don't have here.\n\nHow it behaves:\n- **Index missing:** creates it.\n- **Same name, same fields:** returns nil and changes nothing, so running it twice is safe.\n- **Same name, different fields:** returns `ErrConflict` and changes nothing.\n- **Another process creates the index between the check and the create:** `CreateIndex` returns `ErrExists`, and `EnsureIndex` compares the fields again instead of failing.\n\nThe field comparison counts order, so an index over (a, b) conflicts with one over (b, a). In a composite index, the order changes what the index is. A single `CreateIndex` call either succeeds or fails completely, so a crash cannot leave half an index behind.\n\n`zz_test.go` is a scratch test I wrote. It checks create, the repeat call, the conflict, and that the index is unchanged afterwards. Run `go test ./...`, then delete the file.",
